;\n    }}\n    on:mousedown={() => size.set(30)}\n    on:mouseup={() => size.set(10)}\n>\n    <circle\n        cx={$coords.x}\n        cy={$coords.y}\n        r={$size}\n        role=\"button\" <!-- or \"link\", \"image\", or an appropriate role -->\n    />\n</svg>\n```\n\nIn this example, I've used the \"button\" role as an example because it behaves like an interactive element, but you can choose an appropriate role based on the purpose of your pointer. The \"link\" role might also be suitable if the pointer represents a link or an action.\n\nRemember to choose the ARIA role that best describes the functionality of your SVG element to enhance its accessibility for users of assistive technologies.","turn_id":"turn_000003"},"target_developer_prompt":{"create_time":1698328988.023419,"event_index":2,"role":"user","source_node_id":"aaa2f993-d2bc-4f6a-9c11-4fcdf3fe4aee","source_parent_id":"4fd49f6e-6f57-4705-acab-2466eb1d9341","source_record_index":2,"text":"What is the correct aria-role for this svg which acts as a pointer?\n```svelte\n<svg\n\ton:mousemove={(e) => {\n\t\tcoords.set({ x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY });\n\t}}\n\ton:mousedown={() => size.set(30)}\n\ton:mouseup={() => size.set(10)}\n>\n\t<circle\n\t\tcx={$coords.x}\n\t\tcy={$coords.y}\n\t\tr={$size}\n\t/>\n</svg>\n```","turn_id":"turn_000002"}},"csv_extraction":{"context":[{"category":"context","evidence_spans":["What is the correct aria-role for this svg which acts as a pointer?","on:mousemove={(e) => {\n\t\tcoords.set({ x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY });\n\t}}","on:mousedown={() => size.set(30)}","on:mouseup={() => size.set(10)}"],"item_id":"context_1","normalized_text":"A Svelte SVG acts as a pointer and handles mouse movement and button events; mouse movement updates `coords`, mouse down sets `size` to 30, and mouse up sets `size` to 10.","source_roles":["user"],"source_turn_ids":["turn_000002"]}],"specificity":[{"category":"specificity","evidence_spans":["What is the correct aria-role for this svg which acts 